Job Finder India — NOTICE
How your data & credentials are handled
========================================

1. Your AI assistant's credentials
   Scoring runs inside the AI CLI you already use (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, ...),
   under that assistant's own login. This tool never sees, stores, or transmits your
   model credentials, and it holds no AI API key of its own.

2. Job data
   Job postings come from free, public APIs: the documented ATS APIs (Greenhouse,
   Lever, Ashby, Workable, SmartRecruiters), the official Adzuna API, and — for
   Workday — the same public, keyless JSON endpoints its own careers pages use
   (undocumented but publicly served; accessed at low volume, with an identifying
   User-Agent, and never around a block). Optionally, third-party APIs you enable
   with your own keys (JSearch, SerpAPI, Apify) add coverage; those providers do
   their own collection under their own terms. This tool does not scrape websites
   that block automated access: blocked sites are detected and skipped, never
   worked around.

3. Your résumé and profile
   resume.md, config/profile.yml, config/preferences.yml, .env, and everything under
   data/ stay on your machine. They are excluded from version control (.gitignore)
   and are never uploaded by this tool. The only content that leaves your machine is
   the job text your own AI assistant reads in order to score it, under that
   assistant's terms.

See DATA_CONTRACT.md for the full data contract, and LICENSE for the license (MIT).
